msgstr "Показывать две панели папок рядом"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:9
msgid ""
"Spiral is a GTK4 and libadwaita file manager for Wayland desktops that come "
"without one. It follows the layout and behaviour of GNOME Files and adds a "
"file chooser portal backend, so applications that open and save files "
"through the portal get the same picker."
msgstr ""
"Spiral — файловый менеджер на GTK4 и libadwaita для окружений Wayland, в "
"которых его нет. Он повторяет компоновку и поведение Файлов GNOME и "
"добавляет бэкенд портала выбора файлов, поэтому приложения, открывающие и "
"сохраняющие файлы через портал, получают тот же диалог."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:11
msgid ""
"Grid, list and column views, tabs, and a places sidebar with devices, "
"bookmarks and favorites"
msgstr ""
"Виды сетки, списка и столбцов, вкладки и боковая панель с устройствами, "
"закладками и избранным"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:12
msgid ""
"Copy, move, trash, rename and duplicate with progress, conflict handling and "
"undo"
msgstr ""
"Копирование, перемещение, удаление в корзину, переименование и дублирование "
"с индикацией хода, разрешением конфликтов и отменой"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:13
msgid "Archive extraction and creation with the tools installed on the system"
msgstr ""
"Распаковка и создание архивов с помощью установленных в системе инструментов"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:14
msgid "Sandboxed thumbnails, drag and drop, and \"Open in Terminal\""
msgstr ""
"Изолированное создание миниатюр, перетаскивание и «Открыть в терминале»"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:15
msgid ""
"The org.freedesktop.FileManager1 service, so browsers and chat apps can show "
"a file in its folder"
msgstr ""
"Служба org.freedesktop.FileManager1, чтобы браузеры и мессенджеры могли "
"показать файл в его папке"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:22
msgid "sachesi"
msgstr "sachesi"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:27
msgid ""
"Colour tags, off until \"Colour Tags\" in Preferences turns them on. A tag "
"is a name and a colour; seven come by default, and the ones you make take a "
"colour from the palette or one of your own. A file's tags live in its "
"user.xdg.tags attribute, so they survive renames, moves and copies and are "
"the tags Dolphin and Baloo read; an index under the user data dir says which "
"files carry each tag, since nothing can ask every file on the disk, and it "
"is corrected as listings show what is true. The context menu tags a "
"selection from a row of coloured dots, the tags of a file lead its name in "
"every view, the list and the columns wash the row with the first colour "
"while the grid washes the name, and the sidebar lists the tags, opens what "
"carries one, takes drops to tag files, and renames, recolours and removes "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:28
msgid ""
"\"Copy to…\", \"Move to…\" and \"Extract To…\" ask in a dialog attached to "
"the window instead of a file chooser window of its own: folders and nothing "
"else, \"New Folder\" in the header for a destination that does not exist "
"yet, and the button takes the folder selected or the one on screen. The "
"dialog folds its sidebar away in a narrow window and has a button to ask it "
"back, as the portal chooser now does at its own width. Ctrl+L types a "
"location in the dialogs as well as in the window, and the portal chooser "
"answers Ctrl+R, F5 and Ctrl+S from anywhere in it. A drop on a folder in the "
"list or the columns goes into the folder under the pointer, which is tinted "
"while the drag is over it, and files dropped on Trash are trashed whether "
"the drag arrived as a move or a copy."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:29
msgid ""
"A video preview goes on playing when the arrows step to the next file, and a "
"sound file whose length is only known once the pipeline has read into it "
"gets its timeline and the seeking that comes with it. Ctrl+S no longer picks "
"files out by pattern in a save dialog, where that key belongs to the "
"application the dialog was opened for, and \"Empty Trash…\" does not ask its "
"question over an empty trash."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:30
msgid ""
"Opening in a new tab, a new window or a terminal are items of the menu again "
"rather than a submenu, and the colours of a tag are a row of dots in its "
"menu, since a menu that has had a submenu open is not dismissed by a click "
"outside it. Which of the optional entries a context menu carries is a page "
"of its own in Preferences, which are laid out as pages now that there are "
"enough of them: opening in a new tab or a new window, \"Copy to…\", \"Move "
"to…\", \"Create Link\" and \"Delete Permanently\" are all off to begin with, "
"and a middle click still opens a folder in a new tab whatever the menu shows."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:31
msgid ""
"Servers, wherever gvfs has a backend for one. \"Connect to Server…\" in the "
"main menu takes an address, names the schemes the system can actually use, "
"and offers the servers connected to before. A share that answers opens in a "
"tab and joins the sidebar under Network, above it the machines gvfs can find "
"and beside it a button that disconnects it again. Going to a share that is "
"not connected connects it first, so a bookmark or an address typed into the "
"path bar reaches the server without the dialog being opened at all. Without "
"gvfs there are no network locations, and Spiral says so rather than offer an "
"address it has no way to open, and \"Network Locations\" in Preferences "
"takes the whole of it away for those who have no server to reach."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:36
msgid ""
"Renaming takes a whole selection: F2 on several files opens a dialog that "
"gives them all a shared name with numbers after it, or replaces some text of "
"the old names with other text, listing the names it would give as the rule "
"is typed and refusing to rename while two of them would collide. The lot is "
"one entry in the operations list and one undo. \"New Document\" offers what "
"is in the templates folder, a document per file and a submenu per folder, "
"and both it and \"New Folder…\" ask for a name before they make anything, "
"with everything but the extension selected."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:37
msgid ""
"A drag held for a moment over a folder, a breadcrumb or a sidebar entry "
"opens it, so files can be carried somewhere that is not on screen when the "
"drag starts, and files dropped on Trash are trashed. Ctrl+S selects the "
"names matching a pattern and Ctrl+Shift+I turns the selection round. Escape "
"stops a folder or a search that is still coming in and keeps what has "
"arrived, Ctrl+0 is normal size, and Alt with a digit goes to that tab from "
"anywhere in the window. Folders open in a new window as well as a new tab, a "
"device met in a folder can be unmounted or ejected from there, and the ways "
"of opening are gathered under one entry so the menu of a file is shorter. A "
"folder opened now takes the keyboard with it, and submenus open beside their "
"item instead of moving the menu out from under the pointer."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:38
msgid ""
"The file chooser searches the folder it is showing, and only that one, and "
"sorts from its header; it keeps the view and the order it was left in apart "
"from the file manager's own. Answers that cost the disk — which terminals "
"are installed, what the bookmarks file says, whether gvfs keeps per-folder "
"metadata — are no longer fetched again on every change of the selection, and "
"a picture from a share is decoded where a picture from the disk already was, "
"off the thread drawing the window."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:43
msgid ""
"Big folders open in a fraction of the time and scroll without stutter. A "
"folder that does not fit in one batch of its listing is shown once, complete "
"and in order, instead of arriving unsorted and being replaced twice; only "
"the view on screen holds the folder, so the two views not showing no longer "
"bind every row it changes; the grid keeps cells for the columns that fit the "
"window rather than for the twenty it may ever have; and a cell's tooltip is "
"answered when the pointer asks instead of being set on every bind, which "
"cost a style lookup per cell. Opening a folder of three thousand photos "
"takes a fifth of the processor time it took on the thread drawing the window."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:44
msgid ""
"Thumbnails are asked for only once their cell is on screen and the folder is "
"in order, and a screenful is made from the top down rather than in the order "
"the cells happened to be bound. A thumbnailer that ran out of time or could "
"not be started leaves no note, so the file is tried again on the next visit; "
"only the notes Spiral left itself are read, not those gnome-desktop leaves; "
"and where several thumbnailers claim a type they are taken by name and tried "
"in turn, so one that lacks a codec hands the file to the next. Pictures "
"larger than a limit in the settings are left with their icon, a thumbnailer "
"stands aside for the window it draws into, and the debug log accounts for "
"every request."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:45
msgid ""
"Text in the preview has line numbers, on the colour of the page. A video "
"opens in its own proportions, read from the header of its container when the "
"cache holds no thumbnail, instead of snapping to them once it plays. An "
"application whose desktop entry asks for a terminal is given the one from "
"Preferences, so a terminal editor works as a default."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:50
msgid ""
"Bubblewrap is now required. Thumbnailers, the PDF previewer and the archive "
"tools are decoders fed files nobody here wrote, and all three used to run "
"unconfined where bubblewrap was missing, while images with no thumbnailer of "
"their own were decoded inside the window itself. None of that happens any "
"more: without the sandbox they are not run, and Spiral tries it once at "
"startup and says what is wrong with it rather than showing nothing. A "
"thumbnailer or a PDF tool that stops answering is killed after twenty "
"seconds instead of holding a slot for the rest of the session."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:51
msgid ""
"Big folders open in about half the processor time they took. A folder is put "
"in order once, when its listing ends, instead of after each batch of files "
"arrives; names are collated once each instead of once per comparison; a "
"thumbnail is looked for when a row is shown instead of for every file in the "
"folder, listed or not; a burst of changes in a folder is answered in one "
"pass; and the selection is read out once a frame rather than on every motion "
"of a rubber band. Item counts under grid icons are remembered, and searching "
"file contents no longer does its reading and matching on the thread drawing "
"the window. The thumbnail cache keeps to a size instead of emptying itself, "
"and generation uses the cores there are."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:56
msgid ""
"The sidebar gained Root, the top of the filesystem, and a switch in "
"Preferences for it and for Favorites. The order folders open in can be "
"chosen in Preferences instead of only by sorting one, and a folder that "
"remembers an order of its own still keeps it. Caption lines chosen in the "
"dialog appear at once. The selection is no longer lost when a file in the "
"folder is written, so a pasted screenshot keeps the selection it was given. "
"The star column is as narrow as the star it holds, whatever the word for it "
"in the language of the moment, and an empty star is faded so it reads as "
"empty under any icon theme."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:61
msgid ""
"The column view is now optional and starts turned off: with it off the view "
"button and the view menu offer the grid and the list alone. Pasted files, "
"folders and screenshots are selected once they land in the folder. Source "
"code in the preview is coloured, on the window's own background, and text "
"files keep their lines unwrapped. The list drops the columns beside the name "
"as a window narrows, so a name is never squeezed into an ellipsis, and shows "
"the whole of one that had to be cut when the pointer rests on it. "
"Preferences are grouped by what they change, and Tab in the location bar no "
"longer takes the focus away from a half-typed path."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:66
msgid ""
"Column view no longer decides the view of every folder after it: a folder "
"that remembers a view of its own gets it back, while columns still survive a "
"move that has nothing else to say. Where the system cannot keep a setting "
"with each folder, that choice now falls to the global default instead of "
"going nowhere at all, and the preference says as much. Opening a window or a "
"tab no longer writes the zoom settings back over themselves, and the program "
"is half the size it was."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:71
msgid ""
"A quick preview on the Space key: images, PDFs a page at a time, video, "
"sound and text with source code among it, drawn by Spiral itself in a window "
"that takes the proportions of what it holds before it opens rather than "
"resizing in front of you. The arrows walk the folder without leaving the "
"preview, Page Up and Page Down turn the pages of a PDF, Return hands the "
"file to its application, and Ctrl with the wheel zooms a picture around the "
"pointer, which is then moved by dragging it. Video and sound play through "
"one GStreamer pipeline kept for the whole session, and a sound file shows "
"the cover it carries whether or not a thumbnailer ever saw it. A middle "
"click opens a folder in a new tab, the first arrow key in a folder selects "
"its first item, and a photograph is turned the way the camera held it. "
"Windows, tabs and dialogs let go of everything they held when they close."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:76
msgid ""
"A column view, the third way to look at a folder: the path drawn as a strip "
"of lists, one folder per column, with the folder you are in at the right and "
"whatever the selection points at beside it. One click in any other column "
"goes there. Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2 and Ctrl+3 now name a view instead of two keys "
"toggling. Shift and the wheel move the strip sideways, and a drag held near "
"either end pushes it along, so a column off the screen can still be dropped "
"on. A file written after it is created, an image pasted from the clipboard "
"say, gets its thumbnail without a restart."
msgstr ""
"Вид столбцов — третий способ смотреть на папку: путь нарисован полосой "
"списков, по папке на столбец, текущая папка справа, а рядом с ней то, на что "
"указывает выделение. Один щелчок в любом другом столбце переходит туда. "
"Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2 и Ctrl+3 теперь называют вид, а не переключают два. Shift с "
"колесом двигает полосу вбок, а перетаскивание у её края толкает её дальше, "
"так что на столбец за экраном всё равно можно бросить файлы. Файл, который "
"записывают после создания, например вставленный из буфера снимок экрана, "
"получает миниатюру без перезапуска."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:81
msgid ""
"A click on empty space in a folder takes the keyboard and clears the "
"selection, so Ctrl+A and the other file keys no longer wait for a file to be "
"clicked; the keyboard also comes back after a menu closes and after the "
"navigation buttons. A right click on empty space keeps the selection, and "
"the menu it opens acts on the folder. The search filters button has an icon "
"again."
msgstr ""
"Щелчок по пустому месту в папке передаёт ей клавиатуру и снимает выделение, "
"поэтому Ctrl+A и остальные клавиши для файлов больше не ждут, пока будет "
"выбран файл; клавиатура возвращается и после закрытия меню, и после кнопок "
"навигации. Щелчок правой кнопкой по пустому месту сохраняет выделение, а "
"открытое им меню действует на папку. У кнопки фильтров поиска снова есть "
"значок."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:86
msgid ""
"Two folder panes side by side, off by default and turned on with F3: F6 "
"moves between them, the pane in charge is outlined, and everything outside "
"the view acts on that one. Dropping files asks whether to copy, move or "
"link, which Preferences can turn off. An up button beside back and forward. "
"\"Show in folder\" from a browser no longer waits twenty-five seconds on a "
"portal deadlock, and opens a window of its own with the file selected."
msgstr ""
"Две панели папок рядом, по умолчанию выключены и включаются по F3: F6 "
"переключает между ними, активная панель обведена, и всё за пределами области "
"просмотра действует именно на неё. При перетаскивании файлов Spiral "
"спрашивает, копировать, переместить или создать ссылку; в параметрах это "
"можно отключить. Кнопка «вверх» рядом с кнопками назад и вперёд. «Показать в "
"папке» из браузера больше не ждёт двадцать пять секунд из-за взаимной "
"блокировки портала и открывает отдельное окно с выделенным файлом."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:91
msgid ""
"A new application icon. Files cut to the clipboard are faded until they are "
"pasted, and an image on the clipboard, a screenshot say, pastes into the "
"folder as a PNG. The clipboard keys work with the focus anywhere in the "
"window. Drags start anywhere on a row or grid tile and folders accept a drop "
"across their whole row. Compact, resizable list columns with the type shown "
"as the file extension, and a star toggle that follows the favourites."
msgstr ""
"Новый значок приложения. Файлы, вырезанные в буфер обмена, показываются "
"приглушёнными до вставки, а изображение из буфера обмена, например снимок "
"экрана, вставляется в папку в виде PNG. Клавиши буфера обмена работают при "
"фокусе в любом месте окна. Перетаскивание начинается в любой части строки "
"или плитки, и папки принимают перетаскивание по всей строке. Компактные "
"столбцы списка с изменяемой шириной, тип показан как расширение файла, "
"переключатель звёздочки следует за избранным."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:96
msgid ""
"Search walks subfolders, filters by type and date and can match file "
"contents. Visible columns and captions dialogs, expandable folders in the "
"list view. Restore from trash, links, Copy to and Move to, Run as a Program, "
"path bar and tab context menus, tabs moved between windows and restored "
"after closing. Password-protected archives. Lock emblems and greyed actions "
"for read-only files, folders that follow outside changes, and the clipboard "
"pastes paths into terminals."
msgstr ""
"Поиск обходит подпапки, фильтрует по типу и дате и умеет искать по "
"содержимому файлов. Диалоги видимых столбцов и подписей, разворачиваемые "
"папки в списке. Восстановление из корзины, ссылки, «Копировать в» и "
"«Переместить в», запуск как программы, контекстные меню строки пути и "
"вкладок, перенос вкладок между окнами и восстановление закрытых. Архивы с "
"паролем. Эмблемы замка и недоступные действия для файлов только для чтения, "
"папки следят за изменениями извне, а буфер обмена вставляет пути в терминалы."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:101
msgid ""
"Russian and Ukrainian translations. Sort order remembered per folder. A "
"Nautilus-style command line: new windows per call, -w, -s, -q. Filesystem "
"calls no longer block the interface on slow mounts."
msgstr ""
"Русский и украинский переводы. Порядок сортировки запоминается для каждой "
"папки. Командная строка в стиле Nautilus: новое окно на каждый вызов, -w, "
"-s, -q. Обращения к файловой системе больше не блокируют интерфейс на "
"медленных точках монтирования."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:105
msgid "First release."
msgstr "Первый выпуск."

